{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9uyUCMY2LmytkL1B9x5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`--and` patterns now get the same path-separator check as the main pattern. Before, only the main pattern was checked, so `fd foo --and one/two` quietly returned nothing; now it fails with the same error naming the bad pattern. `--full-path` still turns the check off for all patterns.\n\nThe full test suite passes, including a new test for this case. Clippy reports nothing new: all its warnings are old ones in `tests/tests.rs` about redundant `&` in `format!`.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`src/main.rs`:** the check for one pattern is now its own function, `ensure_pattern_is_not_a_path(pattern: &str)`. `ensure_search_pattern_is_not_a_path` returns early under `--full-path`, then runs that check on the main pattern and each `--and` pattern, stopping at the first one that fails. The Windows-only check (a `\\` pattern that names an existing directory) now applies to `--and` patterns too.\n- **`tests/tests.rs`:** added `test_and_pattern_with_forward_slash_is_rejected`. It checks that `fd foo --and one/two` gives the error and that adding `--full-path` makes it succeed.\n\nThe changes aren't committed yet (the checkout is on a detached HEAD). I can commit them with your message as the subject if you want."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":716,"cache_read_input_tokens":37273,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":716,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8abb002b-4573-4079-965b-c4601814df49","uuid":"41c6016f-8234-4b31-bae4-cad3c8c022be","timestamp":"2026-10-18T15:09:25.101Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9uyTziEvRPJgqLfuyHT"}
